        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Girlguiding North West England\n- Places: Preston, Lancashire; River Ribble; Cumberland; Westmorland; Cheshire; Lancashire; Isle of Man; City of Preston\n- Topics: regional coverage; local government geography\n\nFacts:\n- In 1960, Girlguiding North West England was introduced.\n- In 1960, Girlguiding North West England covered the counties of Cumberland, Westmorland, Cheshire, and Lancashire, plus the Isle of Man.\n- In 1960, Girlguiding North West England had its headquarters in Preston.\n- Preston is on the north bank of the River Ribble.\n- Preston is an urban settlement and unparished area in Lancashire.\n- Preston, together with surrounding rural civil parishes, forms the City of Preston local government district of Lancashire.",
